  annotation "note_1771576586055_1", anchor: "too clean for impact damage", text: "Fire-core crystals fracture along thermal stress lines. A crack this precise suggests controlled quenching — deliberate cooling at a rate no battlefield impact would produce. The ice-memory at Midway Shelf is badly degraded by corruption bleed from the Glow-Fissure's northern reach, but what thermal signatures I could recover do not support an impact event at the forge. Someone broke this amulet on purpose. That changes the sentence it appears in.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576586055_2", anchor: "at the cost of the practitioner's own memory. Dual mastery", text: "Shawl☽ Sun hollows memories. Star∴eternal demands the fire never sleep. He practices both. He read the Mist~Record. He is Touched. Every capacity he possesses is consuming him from a different direction, and he has arranged the terms of his own expenditure with a merchant's precision. I wrote in the next section that what he purchased remains unclear. I am less certain of that than the main text allows me to say.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576586055_3", anchor: "records him among its celebrated figures", text: "An incomplete utterance, preserved by a law that makes memory compulsory. The Accord cannot let him finish and cannot let him stop.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576586055_4", anchor: "the forge at Midway Shelf, where the seventeen courier-law violators still stand as skeletons", text: "The skeletons are at Midway Shelf. The forge was adjacent but distinct — a temporary installation for emergency fire-core processing during the Incursion. The distance between them is roughly forty body-lengths of open ice. Someone walked that distance. The entry compresses the geography; the walk should not be compressed.", type: :correction, display: :popout
